# 🐛 bug report

(Works fine in dev mode)

## 🤔 Expected Behavior

Chrome 75 doesn't support module workers, so the worker bundle shouldn't be ESM.

## 😯 Current Behavior

The output contains `new Worker` without `type: module` but the worker bundle has `import "...";` declarations.

## 💻 Code Sample

```html
<script type="module" src="index.js"></script>
```
```js
// index.js
import x from "./lib.js";
console.log(x);
new Worker("./worker.js", { type: "module" });

// worker.js
import x from "./lib.js";
console.log(x);

// lib.js
export default 1235;
```

package.json:
```json
{
	"browserslist": "Chrome 75",
	"@parcel/bundler-default": {
		"minBundleSize": 0
	}
}
```

